        "original_id": "d499698e-33db-5f95-8f85-c0e04f2ab66b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Polly Draper, Tim Roth, Nat and Alex Wolff, Boris Pelekh\n- Works: Thirtysomething, The Hit, The Naked Brothers Band\n- Organizations: ABC, Nickelodeon, Gogol Bordello\n\nFacts:\n- Tim Roth was born on 14 May 1961 and is an English actor and director.\n- Tim Roth garnered critical acclaim for playing Myron in the 1984 film The Hit and received his first BAFTA Award nomination for that role.\n- Polly Draper first gained recognition for her role in the ABC primetime television drama Thirtysomething, which ran from 1987 to 1991.\n- Nat and Alex Wolff are siblings known for their work on the Nickelodeon television series The Naked Brothers Band.\n- Polly Draper created and produced The Naked Brothers Band and is the mother of Nat and Alex Wolff.\n- Boris Pelekh worked with the Nickelodeon duo Nat and Alex Wolff from 2008 to 2011, in addition to his work with Gogol Bordello.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
